<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/01M5">Definition <span data-tag="01M5">6.3.0.1</span>.</a> Let $F: \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}\rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{D}}$ be a functor between categories and let $W$ be a collection of morphisms of $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$. We say that $F$ <em>exhibits $\operatorname{\mathcal{D}}$ as a strict localization of $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ with respect to $W$</em> if, for every category $\operatorname{\mathcal{E}}$, precomposition with $F$ induces a bijection </p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix@R =50pt@C=50pt{ \{  \textnormal{Functors $\operatorname{\mathcal{D}}\rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{E}}$} \}  \ar [d] \\ \{  \textnormal{Functors $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}\rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{E}}$ carrying each $w \in W$ to an isomorphism in $\operatorname{\mathcal{E}}$} \}  .} \]
</div>
